$ go run ./cmd/coimnet run --help
2026/09/17 00:11:12 [insyra - Info] Welcome to Insyra Huashan(v0.3.2)!!
Official website: https://insyra.hazelnut-paradise.com

Usage: coimnet run --config FILE [--set section.field=value]... --dry-run
Reads one strictly validated coimnet-config/v1 document and expands it over four layers, in the fixed order default, file, environment (COIMNET_SECTION_FIELD), command line (--set). Unknown fields, duplicate keys, null required values and names no implementation answers to are all refused. A secret is only ever a reference of the form {"ref": "env:NAME"}; its value is never read or printed here.
With --dry-run it resolves the task generator, loads the declared model package or graph store, builds the pre-launch memory estimate and checks it against resources.max_memory_mib, then prints one coimnet-dry-run/v1 JSON document holding the expanded configuration, the provenance of every leaf, every check and the estimate with its formulas. A dry run has no side effects: it writes no file, creates no output directory, changes no parameter and calls no teacher.
Without --dry-run the command reports that executing a configuration is not implemented in this stage.
Exit status: 0 when every check passes, 2 when the run is refused (a failed check, or an estimate above the declared limit), 1 for a usage or configuration error.
Example: coimnet run --config runs/fixture.json --set resources.max_memory_mib=4096 --dry-run > dry-run.json
Errors: missing or unreadable configuration, invalid or unknown configuration fields, an override that addresses no field, an unreadable model package or graph store, an estimate above the declared memory limit, cancellation or output failure.
Options and their defaults:
  -config string
    	required path to a coimnet-config/v1 document (default none)
  -dry-run
    	expand and check the configuration without running anything (default false)
  -set value
    	override one field, written section.field=value; repeatable, highest precedence (default none)
